{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeLiterature","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeLiterature","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolumeSqueeze"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_saddle_volume","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaev_saddle_volume","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeLiterature.lean#L57-L62","doc":"The keystone Re-face, now fully unconditional and sorry-free: the Kashaev\nroot-of-unity saddle reproduces the figure-eight hyperbolic volume. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.volumeConjecture41_of_literature","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.volumeConjecture41_of_literature","kind":"instance","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeLiterature.lean#L39-L55","doc":"**The figure-eight volume conjecture, machine-proved** (Kashaev–Murakami–\nMurakami statement for `4₁`; proved in the literature by Andersen–Hansen /\nOhtsuki, and proved HERE, sorry-free, by the saddle program's Riemann-sum\nsqueeze `tendsto_log_kashaev_vol` — `FigureEightVolumeSqueeze.lean`).\n\nHISTORY. Until 2026-07-26 this instance was a cited `sorry` (the\nestablished-in-the-literature encoding), with two obstructions: (a) the\nsaddle asymptotic was unformalized, and (b) `VOL_4_1` was a truncated\nrational decimal ≈ 1e-30 away from `2·Cl₂(π/3)`, making the statement\nliterally false. (b) was repaired by bean qou-yf47 (exact\n`VOL_4_1 = 2·Cl₂(π/3)`); (a) was closed by bricks E1–E5d (milestone\nqou-cpfn): E5a log-bridge, E4/E5c Riemann-sum-vs-Clausen deviation with\nk-uniform master error `E(N) → 0`, the E2/E3 Cl₂ extremum at `5π/3`, and\nthe E5d two-envelope squeeze. No Borel resummation was needed — the\nroot-of-unity Kashaev sum for `4₁` admits this elementary route. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaev_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.log_kashaev_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/FigureEightVolumeLiterature.lean#L33-L37","doc":"`log ⟨4₁⟩_N ≥ 0` for `N ≥ 1` — sorry-free glue from the `kashaev_ge_one`\nfloor: the sequence whose limit the volume conjecture asserts is\nnon-negative termwise. ","signatureChunk":0}]}